\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. HOW happy every child of grace,
\par Who knows his sins forgiven!
\par This earth, he cries, is not my place,
\par I seek my place in heaven!
\par A country far from mortal sight;
\par Yet O by faith I see
\par The land of rest, the saint's delight,
\par The heaven prepared for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A stranger in the world below,
\par I calmly sojourn here;
\par Nor can its happiness or woe
\par Provoke my hope or fear;
\par Its evils in a moment end,
\par Its joys as soon are past;
\par But O the bliss to which I tend
\par Eternally shall last.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To that Jerusalem above
\par With singing I repair;
\par While in the flesh, my hope and love,
\par My heart and soul, are there;
\par There my exalted Saviour stands,
\par My merciful High-priest,
\par And still extends His wounded hands
\par To take me to His breast
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O what a blessed hope in ours,
\par While hear on earth we stay,
\par We more than taste the heavenly powers,
\par And antedate that day;
\par We feel the resurrection near,
\par Our life in Christ concealed,
\par And with His glorious presence here
\par Our earthen vessels filled.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

